texts.en:
1 Before the insurance contract is concluded, the insurance company must inform the policyholder comprehensibly, and in a form that allows proof by text, of its identity and of the essential content of the insurance contract. It must provide information on:¹²
a. the insured risks;
b.¹³ the scope of the insurance cover and whether it is fixed-sum insurance or indemnity insurance;
c. the premiums owed and the other duties of the policyholder;
d. the term and termination of the insurance contract;
e. the calculation bases and the distribution principles and methods that apply to determining surpluses and to surplus participation;
f.¹⁴ the surrender and conversion values and the main types of cost associated with a surrenderable life insurance in the event of surrender;
g.¹⁵ the processing of personal data, including the purpose and type of the database and the recipients and retention of the data;
h.¹⁶ the right of withdrawal under Article 2a and the form and time limit for withdrawal;
i.¹⁷ a time limit for submitting the notice of loss under Article 38 paragraph 1;
j.¹⁸ the temporal validity of the insurance cover, in particular in cases where the insured event occurs during the term of the contract but the resulting loss occurs only after the contract has ended;
k.¹⁹ the qualification of a life insurance as a qualified life insurance under Article 39a of the Versicherungsaufsichtsgesetz of 17 December 2004²⁰ (VAG).

2 This information must be given to the policyholder in such a way that the policyholder can know it when proposing or accepting the insurance contract. In any case, the policyholder must at that time be in possession of the general insurance conditions and of the information under paragraph 1 letter g.

3 If an employer takes out collective personal insurance to protect its employees, it is obliged to inform the employees, in writing or in another form that allows proof by text, of the essential content of the contract and of its changes and termination. The insurance company must provide the employer with the documents required for this purpose.²¹

¹² Amended by No. I of the Federal Act of 19 June 2020, in force since 1 Jan. 2022 (AS 2020 4969; BBl 2017 5089).

