texts.en:
1 The duty to report applies to:
a. higher education institutions under Article 2 paragraph 2 of the Hochschulförderungs- und -koordinationsgesetz of 30 September 2011⁵⁵;
b. federal, cantonal and communal authorities and intercantonal, cantonal and intercommunal organisations, with the exception of the Gruppe Verteidigung when the army is performing assistance service under Article 67 or active service under Article 76 of the Militärgesetz of 3 February 1995⁵⁶;
c. organisations with public-law tasks in the areas of security and rescue, drinking water supply, wastewater treatment and waste disposal;
d. enterprises active in the areas of energy supply under Article 6 paragraph 1 of the Energiegesetz of 30 September 2016⁵⁷, energy trading, energy metering or energy control, with the exception of licence holders under the Kernenergiegesetz of 21 March 2003⁵⁸ where a cyberattack is made on a nuclear installation;
e. enterprises subject to the Bankengesetz of 8 November 1934⁵⁹, the Versicherungsaufsichtsgesetz of 17 December 2004⁶⁰ or the Finanzmarktinfrastrukturgesetz of 19 June 2015⁶¹;
f. healthcare institutions included in the cantonal list of hospitals under Article 39 paragraph 1 letter e of the Federal Act of 18 March 1994⁶² über die Krankenversicherung;
g. medical laboratories with a licence under Article 16 paragraph 1 of the Epidemiengesetz of 28 September 2012⁶³;
h. enterprises that hold a licence under the Heilmittelgesetz of 15 December 2000⁶⁴ for the manufacture, placing on the market and import of medicinal products;
i. organisations that provide benefits to protect against the consequences of illness, accident, incapacity for work and for gainful employment, old age, disability and helplessness;
j. the Schweizerische Radio- und Fernsehgesellschaft;
k. news agencies of national importance;
l. postal service providers registered with the Postkommission under Article 4 paragraph 1 of the Postgesetz of 17 December 2010⁶⁵;
m. railway undertakings under Article 5 or 8c of the Eisenbahngesetz of 20 December 1957⁶⁶ and cableway, trolleybus, bus and shipping undertakings with a concession under Article 6 of the Personenbeförderungsgesetz of 20 March 2009⁶⁷;
n. civil aviation undertakings holding a licence from the Bundesamt für Zivilluftfahrt, and the national airports under the Sachplan Infrastruktur der Luftfahrt;
o. enterprises that carry goods on the Rhine under the Seeschifffahrtsgesetz of 23 September 1953⁶⁸, and enterprises that carry out registration, loading or unloading in the port of Basel;
p. enterprises that supply the population with essential goods for daily needs and whose failure or impairment would lead to considerable supply shortages;
q. telecommunications service providers registered with the Bundesamt für Kommunikation under Article 4 paragraph 1 FMG⁶⁹;
r. registry operators and registrars of internet domains under Article 28b FMG;
s. providers and operators of services and infrastructures used for the exercise of political rights;
t. providers and operators of cloud computing, search engines, digital security and trust services and data centres, provided that they have a registered office in Switzerland;
u. manufacturers of hardware or software whose products are used by critical infrastructures, provided that the hardware or software has remote maintenance access or is used for one of the following purposes:
1. control and monitoring of operational systems and processes,
2. ensuring public safety.

2 For authorities and organisations that also carry out activities not covered by paragraph 1, there is no duty to report cyberattacks that affect exclusively those activities.

3 The duty to report under paragraph 1 applies to cyberattacks that have effects in Switzerland, even if the IT resources affected are located abroad.

