texts.en:
1 Reporting Swiss financial institutions must inform the reportable persons, directly or through their contracting party, no later than 31 January of the year in which information concerning them is first transmitted to a GMS partner state, of:⁷⁹
a. their status as a reporting Swiss financial institution;
b.⁸⁰ the agreements under Article 1 paragraph 1 letters a and b and their content, in particular the information to be exchanged under the agreements;
c. the list of Switzerland's GMS partner states and the place where the current list is published;
d.⁸¹ the use of this information permitted in application of the agreements under Article 1 paragraph 1 letters a and b;
e. the rights of the reportable persons under the DSG⁸² and this Act.

2 For reportable accounts that have been closed, the information must be given once, to the last known address. For accounts that meet the criteria under Article 11 paragraph 6 letter a or b, the information may be omitted.

3 Reporting Swiss financial institutions must publish on their website a list of Switzerland's GMS partner states updated annually on 31 January, or refer to the list of the Eidgenössische Finanzdepartement (EFD).

4 The reporting Swiss financial institution must, on request, send the holder of the account that is the subject of the report a copy of the report.

